$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM S-Aryl Thiocarboxylates 3; General Procedure: An appropriate
diaryliodonium salt 2 (2mmol) was added to a solution of potassium
thiocarboxylate 1 (2mmol) in DMF at 70-80 °C, and the progress of the
reaction was monitored by TLC. After cooling, the mixture was diluted
with water (10 mL) and the product was extracted with Et2O (3 x 10 mL),
washed with water (10 mL) and dried (MgSO4). The solvent was removed in
vacuo and the residue was chromatographed on a column of silica gel using
first petroleum ether (bp 70-90 °C) as eluent, followed by CHCl3 to
afford pure S-aryl thiocarboxylate. The products identified by comparison
of melting points with literature values and by 1H NMR and IR spectral
data. 3c, yield 76%. mp ( °C), found: 64-66; reported: 65-665; IR (KBr) v
(cm-1): 2950, 1680, 1450, 1200, 900, 810, 685, 640; 1H NMR (CDCl3/ TMS)
δ, J (Hz): 2.39 (s, 3H), 7.23- 7.53 (m, 7H), 8.06- 8.08 (m, 2H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hypervalent iodine in synthesis. 5. The reaction between diaryliodonium
salts and thiocarboxylic acid salts: a convenient method for the
synthesis of S-aryl thiocarboxylates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM You, Jinzong; Chen, Zhenchu
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Synthesis (1992), (6), 521-2

