$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 Synthesis of polychlorinated diphenyl
sulfide 3a-3w 1.2.1 Synthesis of compounds 3a-3w Chloro-substituted
thiophenol (1 mmol) dissolved in 10 mL toluene was placed in round bottom
flask, then chloro-substituted iodobenzene (1 mmol), cesium carbonate
(2.5 mmol) and tetrakis(triphenylphosphine)palladium (0.1 mmol) were
added to the reaction flask. The reaction solution was heated up to 112
°C and refluxed for 16 h under nitrogen protection, then cooled to room
temperature. The reaction solution was diluted with 100 mL water, the
water phase was extracted with 20 mL petroleum ether 3 time. The
petroleum ether were combined, dried with anhydrous magnesium sulfate,
filtered and concentrated to give the crude product. The crude product
was purified on silica gel column (300-400 mesh) eluted with petroleum
ether to give the desired product. The product was characterized by
LC-MS, IR and NMR spectra and the melting point of the product was
determined. 3c, 76%, white crystal m.p. 90-93 ℃; 1H NMR (CDCl3, 400 MHz)
δ: 7.01 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H), 7.11-7.16 (m, 2H), 7.22 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 1H),
7.38-7.41 (m, 2H); IR (KBr) ν: 3431, 3081, 1562, 1431, 1407, 1139, 1097,
1037, 819, 777, 569 cm-1.
