$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 4,5-Bis(1-phenylethanethio)phthalonitrile [Pn(SEtPh)2].
1,2-Dichloro-4,5-nitrophthalonitrile (3.00 g, 15.2 mmol) was dissolved in
anhydrous THF (50 mL) under nitrogen atmosphere, and the appropriate
PhEtSH compound (6.20 g, 45.0 mmol) was added. After stirring for 30 min,
finely ground anhydrous potassium carbonate (9.75 g, 70.7 mmol) was added
in portions over 1 h with efficient stirring. The reaction mixture was
stirred at 40 °C for 24 h under nitrogen atmosphere. Then the solution
was poured into ice water (200 mL). The precipitate was filtered off,
washed with water until the filtrate was neutral, and dried in vacuo.
Purification of the product was accomplished by silica gel column
chromatography (eluent: CHCl3:MeOH = 9:1). Rotary evaporation of the
solvent. Pn(SEtPh)2 as a colorless crystalline solid. (a) (R)-Pn(SEtPh)2.
Yield of the compound: 4.58 g (76.2% on the basis of
(R)-1,2-dichloro-4,5-nitrophthalonitrile); 1H NMR(300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 1.65
(d, 3H, -CH3), 4.44 (q, 2H, S-CH-Ph), 7.15- 7.25 (m, 12H, -Ph and Ar);
13C NMR(75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 23.3, 47.2, 111.9, 115.4, 127.1, 128.3, 129.1,
131.8, 141.2, 144.2; FT-IR (KBr, cm-1) 3055, 3024, 2979, 2921, 2865, 2229
(C≡N), 1564, 1493, 1452, 1373, 1350, 1222 (C-S-C), 1100, 1058, 1025, 923,
767, 700, 529. Anal. Calcd for C24H20N2S2: C, 71.96; H, 5.03; N, 6.99%.
Found: C, 72.17; H, 4.87; N, 6.52%.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Formation of Helical J-Aggregate of Chiral Thioether-Derivatized
Phthalocyanine Bound by Palladium(II) at the Toluene/Water Interface
