$DATUM 7,7' -Ethylenedithiodi(ethyl
5,6,8-trifluoro-2-methylchromone-3-carboxylate) (3). Ethanedithiol (0.5
g, 5.32 mmol) and triethylamine (0.3 mL) were added to a solution of
chromone 1 (3 g. 9.87 mmol) in DMSO (60 mL). The reaction mixture was
kept for 10 min. The precipitate that formed was filtered off, washed
with water, dried, and rer from CCI4. Compound 3 was obtained, (see
Tables 1 and 2). Yield 2.5 g, 76%. Molecular formula: C28H2OF6O8S2; Found
(%): C 50.74, H 3.06, F 17.17, Calculated (%): C 50.76, H 3.04, F 17.21;
M.p. 204-206 °C; IR, v /cm-1: 1730 (CO2Et); 1645(C=O);1560 (C=C); 990
(CF); NMR, δ (J/Hz) 1H: 1.39 (t, 3H, OCH2CH3): 2.51 (s, 3H, CH3); 3.27
(s, 2H, SCH2); 4.31 (q, 2H, OCH2CH3); 19F: -143.73 (dd, I F, F-5); -13475
(dd, I F, F-6): -130.16 (dd, 1 F, F-8, J5-6 = 22.0, J5-8 = 16.6).
