$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for Synthesis of Compounds 2
A mixture of substituted 3-bromonitrobenzene (0.01 mol), cuprous
thiophenolate (0.01 mol), pyridine (1.5 mL), and quinoline (10 mL) was
heated with stirring in an oil bath at about 220°C for 2h. The hot
solution was then poured into cracked ice and excess conc. hydrochloric
acid, standing for about 2h. The mixture was extracted with ethyl ether,
and the combined organic layers were dried with anhyd. MgSO4,
concentrated under reduced pressure and purified by column chromatography
on silica gel (petroleum ether) to afford the pure product.
4-Chloro-3-((4-chlorophenyl)thio)-1-nitrobenzene (2d). Yellow solid,
yield 76%. mp 116-118°C; IR (KBr) ν: 1572, 1476, 1445, 1388, 1343, 1294
cm-1. 1H NMR (CDCl3) 87.94 (dd, 1H, J = 2.4, 8.7 Hz), 7.64 (d, 1H, J =
3.0Hz), 7.53 (d, 1H, J = 8.4Hz), 7.47-7.48 (m, 4H). MS, m/e (%): 300 (M+,
10.35), 301 (M+ + 1, 49.05), 299 (M+ - 1, 71.86), 218 (100). HRMS calcd
for C12H7Cl2NO2S: 298.9575. Found: 298.9587.
