$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3.1. General procedure for the synthesis of
3a-3l In a 25-mL beaker, 5 mL of IL was placed; then 5 mol% of CuI and
10mol% of Zn(Pro)2 were added and stirred for0.5 h at 60°C; the mixture
was then cooled to room temperature. This was followed by the addition of
10 mmol of 4-chloro benzaldehyde, 12 mmol of thiophenol, and 20 mmol of
K2CO3 to the IL mixture, heated to 110°C for 10-16h under nitrogen
atmosphere. The cooled mixture was extracted with ether (15 ml x 3),
concentrated under reduced pressure, and the residue was purified by
column chromatography on silica gel with cyclohexane and ethyl acetate
(V: V = 10: 1) as eluent. 3r(2): Yellow crystal (from EtOH). Mp: 79-81
°C. 1H NMR (CDCl3, 300MHz) δ: 6.87, 7.21, 7.33, 7.48, 7.58, 8.21. 13C NMR
(75 MHz, CDCl3): 124.94, 125.71, 128.36, 129.99, 130.09, 131.06, 133.37,
135.87, 139.40, 145.08. IR (KBr) ν: 3099, 1565, 1474, 1453, 1057, 998,
782, 655 cm-1. MS (70eV) m/z (%):231.04 (100), 185.23 (76), 154.15(52),
109.01 (61), 77.02 (67). Anal, calcd. for C12H9NO2S: C 62.32, H 3.92;
found C 63.28, H 3.99.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry, ionic liquid support used, reusable catalysts
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Zn(Pro) 2-promoted CuI-catalyzed synthesis of diphenyl sulfide
derivations in ionic liquid
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Guo, Sheng-Rong; Yuan, Yan-Qin; Wang, Li-Jin
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Sulfur Chemistry (2009), 30(1), 10-16

