$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: (2-nitro-phenyl)-phenyl ether (3a)
(2-nitro-phenyl)-(2,6-di-iso-propylphenyl) sulfide (3l). Following above
procedure, 2,6-di-iso-propylbenzenethiol (4.85 g, 25 mmol), KOH (1.40 g,
25 mmol) and 1-chloro- 2-nitro-benzene (3.94g, 25mmol) were used. 3l
(5.91 g) was obtained as a yellow powder in 75% yield. 1H NMR (300MHz,
CDCl3): δ 8.31 (dd, J = 1.5, 8.4 Hz, 1H, Ar-H); 7.52 (t, J = 7.8, 1H,
Ar-H); 7.29-7.35 (m, 3H, Ar-H); 7.19 (dt, 1H, J = 1.5, 7.2 Hz, Ar-H);
6.64 (dd, 1H, J = 1.2, 8.1 Hz, Ar-H); 3.56 (hepta, 2H, J = 6.6 Hz,
CH(CH3)2); 1.11 (d, 12H, J = 16.5 Hz , CH(CH3)2).
