$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Reaction of phthalonitriles I-IV with thiols
(general procedure). To a solution of 5.0 mmol of phthalonitrile I-IV and
corresponding amount of a thiol (10.0 and 20.0 mmol with I, 10.0 mmol
with II; 5.0, 10.0, and 15.0 mmol with III; and 10.0 mmol with IV) in 20
ml of DMF we added dropwise at 20°C under stirring an equimolar amount of
triethylamine. The reaction mixture was kept at room temperature (I-III)
or at 70 (I) or 80°C (IV) for 45 min and then poured to a saturated
solution of NaCl and extracted with ethyl acetate. The organic layer was
washed with two portions of water, dried over anhydrous Na2SO4, and the
solvent was removed under a vacuum. The residue was subjected to
chromatography on silica gel (eluent benzene, toluene, and ethyl acetate
for the reactions with I and II, III, and IV, respectively). The
resulting crystalline substances were recrystallized from ethanol.
Compound: VIa Compound: XVIIIb Yield: 75.0% mp 211-213°C; Formula:
C30H30N4S2; IR ν CN cm-1: 2228; M + 510.13C NMR (DMSO-d6 ) δC, ppm: 156.8
(CAr-N), 148.3 (CAr-S), 135.7 (CAr'-S), 129.3 (CAr'-H), 127.2 (CAr'-H),
125.9 (CAr'-H), 114.0 (CAr-CN), 112.1 (CN) 52.4 (CH2-N), 25.7(CH2), 23.5
(CH2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
