$DATUM 2-(Methylthio)-4-(trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde To a stirred suspension of
sodium thiomethoxide (0.29 g, 4.1 mmol) in DMF (5 mL) was added a
solution of 2-bromo-4-trifluoromethyl)benzaldehyde (1.0 g, 4.0 mmol) in
DMF (5 mL) dropwise over 30 min. After the addition was complete, the
solution was stirred at room temperature for a further 30 minutes. The
solvent was decanted off and the resulting yellow solid was
recrystallized (Et2O/petrol) to give the sulfide. Yield 1.17 g, 75%, fine
colourless needles. M.p. (Et2O/hexane) 90-92 °C; 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3)
δ 10.17 (s, 1H), 7.96 (d, J= 1 Hz, 1H), 7.67 (dd, J= 8.5, 1 Hz, 1H), 7.37
(d, J= 8.5 Hz, 1H), 2.49 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 189.7,
148.2, 132.1, 129.9 (m), 129.6 (m), 126.2 (q, J= 162 Hz), 124.9, 122.2,
14.8; νmax (film)/cm-1 : 1686, 1610, 1337, 1307, 1257, 1167, 1114, 1090,
825, 692; HRMS (FI)+ 220.0171 (220.0170 calcd. For C9H7F3OS, (M)+).
