$DATUM 7-Phenylthio-6-(triazol-2-yl)benzotetrazine 1,3-dioxide (16).
Benzenethiol (15 mg, 0.14 mmol) and finely divided K2CO3 (15 mg, 0.11
mmol) were added at 20 °C to a stirred solution of
7-bromo-6-(triazol-2-yl)benzotetrazine 1,3-dioxide (15) (31 mg, 0.1 mmol)
in DMF (6 mL). After 20 h, the reaction mixture was diluted with water.
The precipitate that formed was filtered off, washed with water, MeOH,
and Et2O, and dried. The yield of BTDO 16. Yield 25 mg (75%). m.p. 294 °C
(from DMSO). Found (%): C, 49.59; H, 2.66; N, 28.71; S, 9.33. C14H9N7O2S.
Calculated (%): C, 49.55; H, 2.67; N, 28.89; S, 9.45. IR (KBr, ν/cm-1):
1365 s, 1420 s, 1459 s, 1480 m, 1510 m, 1650 m. 1H NMR (DMSO-d6), δ: 7.50
(s, 1 H, H(5)); 7.60 (m, 5 H, Ph); 8.80 (s, 1 H, H(8)); 8.87 (s, 2 H,
triazole). 14N NMR (DMSO-d6), δ: -46 (Δν1/2 = 300 Hz) (N(1), N(3)). MS,
m/z: 339 [M]+.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM safety, potentially explosive
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM An unusual cascade of Sn reactions of benzotetrazine 1,3-dioxide
derivatives
