$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1,2-Benzenedithiol adduct of F8 (4c). To a solution of 1,2-benzenedithiol
(90.6 mg, 0.61 mmol) in anhydrous THF (10 mL) was added 60% sodium
hydride (48.9 mg, 1.22 mmol). The resulting reaction mixture was stirred
at RT for 10 minutes after which F8 (276 mg, 0.55 mmol) was added. The
mixture was stirred at RT overnight and then concentrated to dryness. The
residue was purified by column chromatography (hexanes) to obtain the 4c
(250 mg, 75.1%) as a yellow solid along with a tetrakis-substituted
compound (50 mg, 12.8%) as a brownish solid. : 4c :mp 170-172° C 1H NMR,
δ 7.64 (dd, J 1 = 6.0 Hz, J 2 = 3.3 Hz, 2H), 7.45 (dd, J 1 = 6.0 Hz, J 2
= 3.3 Hz, 2H); 19F NMR, δ -95.0 (d, J = 245, 2F), -98.2 (ddt, , J 1 = 247
Hz, J 2 = 54 Hz, J 3 = 6 Hz, 2F), -100.4 (dd, J 1 = 253 Hz, J 2 = 42 Hz,
2F ), -104.1 (dd, , J 1 = 249 Hz, J 2 = 60 Hz, 2F), -124.6 (m, 2F),
-131.5 (d, J = 41 Hz, 2F), -134.2 (d, J = 54 Hz, 2F); Anal. Calcd for
C22H4F14S2: C 44.16, H 0.67; Found: C 44.49, H 0.63.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, other products also detected
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Reactions of Nucleophiles with Perfluoro[2.2]paracyclophane
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
